## ⚙️ RAM Specifications

| Parameter | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| Memory Type | Single-Port RAM |
| Memory Depth | 8 locations |
| Data Width | 16 bits |
| Address Width | 3 bits |
| Total Capacity | 128 bits |
| Write Operation | Synchronous |
| Read Operation | Asynchronous |
| Reset | Asynchronous |
| Data Bus | 16-bit bidirectional (`inout`) |
| Idle Bus State | High impedance (`Z`) |

---

## 🔌 Port Description

| Port | Direction | Width | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `clk` | Input | 1 bit | Clock signal for write operation |
| `rst` | Input | 1 bit | Asynchronous reset |
| `wr_en` | Input | 1 bit | Write enable |
| `rd_en` | Input | 1 bit | Read enable |
| `add` | Input | 3 bits | Selects one of the 8 memory locations |
| `data` | Inout | 16 bits | Shared read/write data bus |

---

## 🔄 Operating Modes

The RAM operates according to the combination of write enable and read enable signals.

| Operating Mode | wr_en | rd_en | Function |
| :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- |
| Write | 1 | 0 | Stores data at the selected address on the rising clock edge |
| Read | 0 | 1 | Outputs stored data immediately |
| Idle | 0 | 0 | No operation; RAM data bus is high-Z |
| Invalid/Both Enabled | 1 | 1 | No operation; RAM data bus is high-Z |

---

## 🏗️ Design Architecture

The RAM design consists of the following major components:

1. **Memory Array:** Stores 8 words, each containing 16 bits.
2. **Address Decoder:** Selects the memory location based on the 3-bit address.
3. **Write Control Logic:** Enables writing at the rising edge of the clock.
4. **Read Multiplexer:** Selects the stored word corresponding to the input address.
5. **Tri-State Buffer:** Controls whether the RAM drives the shared data bus.
6. **Reset Logic:** Clears all memory locations asynchronously.

