## 📊 Simulation Results

### 1. Successful RAM Verification

The correctly implemented RAM passes all the verification tests.

- All 8 memory locations are checked.
- Random write operations are performed.
- Read data matches the reference memory.
- Error counter remains zero.
- Simulation reports PASS.

<!-- Add RAM_PASS.png here -->

![RAM PASS](screenshots/RAM_PASS.png)

*Figure 2: Simulation console showing successful RAM verification.*

<!-- Add RAM_res.png here -->

![RAM Result](screenshots/RAM_res.png)

*Figure 3: Simulation result showing the error counter remaining at zero.*

### 2. Deliberate Bug Injection

To validate the effectiveness of the self-checking testbench, a deliberate error was introduced into the RAM write condition.

**Original write condition:**

`wr_en && !rd_en`

**Modified faulty write condition:**

`!wr_en && !rd_en`

Due to this modification, the RAM does not perform the intended write operations.

The testbench detects the incorrect memory contents during subsequent read operations.

**Observed Result:**
- 8 errors after the initial write and read sequence.
- 8 additional errors after randomized writes.
- Total errors reported: 16.

<!-- Add RAM_fail.png here -->

![RAM Failure](screenshots/RAM_fail.png)

*Figure 4: Simulation console showing detected failures in the faulty RAM design.*

<!-- Add RAM_resu.png here -->

![RAM Error Count](screenshots/RAM_resu.png)

*Figure 5: Error counter reaching 16 after deliberate fault injection.*

### Results Summary

| Design Condition | Expected Result | Observed Result |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Correct RAM | PASS | PASS |
| Faulty RAM | FAIL | 16 errors detected |
| Correct RAM Error Count | 0 | 0 |
| Faulty RAM Error Count | Greater than 0 | 16 |

